BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Livestream Viewing: Japanese Canadian Monument Opening Ceremony
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T170000
UID:d7f7e3ac5b11cca3d5a548e3700b751a@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:Announcement for unveiling of the Japanese Canadian Monument R
 egistration for the livestream has closed\, confirmations have been sent P
 lease join us at the Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre (JCCC) or Momiji He
 alth Care Society (Momiji) on Saturday\, October 3\, 2026 at 3:30pm EST fo
 r the live streaming of the opening ceremony of the Japanese Canadian Monu
 ment that is taking place in Victoria\, British Columbia. A pre-show progr
 am will begin at 3:30pm\, and the opening ceremony livestream will begin a
 t 4:00pm. Further information per livestream location is outlined below. T
 he Japanese Canadian Monument lists the names of all Japanese Canadians up
 rooted in 1942 AND a second set of names of children born after uprooting 
 and up to and including March 31\, 1949\, after which freedom to return to
  the coast was fully granted. The monument acknowledges the forced disposs
 ession and internment of the community during World War II while celebrati
 ng their resilience and impact on the region. These names and locations en
 graved on the wall provide a stark illustration of a community torn apart 
 by policies that were driven by a confluence of race\, economics\, and pow
 er. To set them in stone here is to ensure they are never again forgotten 
 or marginalized. Light refreshments will be served\, and a souvenir book w
 ill be gifted to all attendees. Please note that capacity will be limited 
 based on location selected ( choice between JCCC and Momiji) . Registratio
 n are closed. For more information\, please refer to https://hcmc.uvic.ca/
 project/monument/ . For any questions\, please reach out to jccc@jccc.on.c
 a . Livestream Event Information at the JCCC: Thank you for joining the JC
 CC at the monument unveiling livestream on Saturday\, October 3\, 2026! Do
 ors will open at 2:30pm EST on October 3\, 2026 for sign in\, and the pre-
 show program and livestream will begin at 3:30pm EST in Kobayashi Hall. Li
 ght refreshments will be served\, and a souvenir book will be gifted to al
 l attendees. Please note that the maximum capacity of the livestream event
  in Kobayashi Hall is 300 guests. Once the registration form reaches maxim
 um capacity\, a waitlist for 50 guests will be monitored. Registrants will
  be contacted via email in September to confirm their entrance status (enr
 olled or waitlist) . Further details will be communicated via email\, e-bl
 ast\, and social media in September. The JCCC will also be replaying the l
 ivestream throughout the evening beginning at 7:00pm EST on October 3\, 20
 26 during Nuit Blanche\, as well as during Issei Day on October 4\, 2026. 
 Registration is not required for Nuit Blanche livestream viewing on Octobe
 r 3\, 2026. To register for Issei Day\, please visit: Issei Day page . A s
 ouvenir book will also be gifted to all Issei Day attendees on October 4\,
  2026. We look forward to seeing you there! Livestream Event Information a
 t Momiji Health Care Society: Momiji would like to welcome our community t
 o watch the livestream of the monument unveiling in Victoria\, BC\, from t
 he comfort of the Yone and Coby Kobayashi Auditorium at Momiji Seniors Res
 idence. Momiji will be providing a small\, boxed meal for the first 150 co
 mmunity members and 70 tenants registered. Once we hit capacity\, a waitli
 st will be created\, and we will be working with the JCCC to ensure that a
 s many people as possible are able to watch the event. Since the event is 
 overlapping with our annual bazaar\, we are inviting attendees to arrive a
 nytime from Noon to 3:00pm and support our annual bazaar before joining th
 e livestream. Further details will be communicated by email and social med
 ia in September.\n\nCategories: Community Event
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
URL:https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/10/livestream-viewing-japanese-canadian-
 monument-opening-ceremony
X-SOURCE:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paradise
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270103T190000
UID:43283f91f18b34c68a346ddc96e9bd68@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:The JCCC Gallery's fall exhibition is Paradise : a multimedia 
 installation by Japanese Canadian artists and longtime family friends Mitc
 hell Akiyama and Emma Nishimura that explores intergenerational inheritanc
 e. Combining print\, video\, and sculpture\, the work reflects on their re
 lationship to the legacy of Japanese Canadian internment experienced by th
 eir paternal grandparents. The exhibition draws on a shared childhood memo
 ry of a summer day in Northern Ontario\, where the artists and their sibli
 ngs built a temporary "Frog Paradise." This moment of play\, shaped by a s
 ense of safety and belonging\, becomes a lens for considering how one grou
 p’s utopia can exist alongside another’s harm. The installation includ
 es video that intercuts footage of this experience with recent visits to f
 ormer internment sites in British Columbia. Bridging personal narrative an
 d historical context\, Paradise examines the forced relocation and incarce
 ration of Japanese Canadians\, tracing how this legacy continues to shape 
 memory\, displacement\, and belonging across generations. Nuit Blanche at 
 the JCCC : October 3 rd at 7pm 7pm — Artist Talk Hear from Mitchell Akiy
 ama and Emma Nishimura as they discuss the ideas\, memories\, and historie
 s behind Paradise ! 9pm — Origami Frog Workshop Join the artists for a h
 ands-on workshop inspired by the exhibition’s "Frog Paradise." Opening R
 eception Please join us on October 25 th from 2 to 4pm Opening Reception\n
 \nCategories: Exhibition
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
URL:https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/10/paradise
X-SOURCE:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nuit Blanche 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261004T070000
UID:5b658333d1a84eec9318ef995cae284a@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us in celebrating Nuit Blanche’s 20 th anniversary – 
 a free all-night celebration of contemporary art that transforms Toronto
 ’s public spaces into unexpected landscapes and animates cultural sites 
 throughout the city. This year’s theme\, Tomorrow’s Memories \, invite
 s you to look back to the artists\, curators\, communities and places that
  defined Nuit Blanche and its twenty-year history. The Japanese Canadian C
 ultural Centre (JCCC) Gallery's fall exhibition\, Paradise \, debuts at Nu
 it Blanche with an Artist Talk and interactive Origami Frog workshop. Para
 dise is a multimedia installation by Japanese Canadian artists and longtim
 e family friends Mitchell Akiyama and Emma Nishimura that explores interge
 nerational inheritance. The JCCC will also host building and museum tours\
 , audio and guided tours\, screenings of the unveiling of the Japanese Can
 adian Monument in Victoria\, British Columbia\, button making\, origami\, 
 lantern workshops\, and more! Learn more at toronto.ca/NuitBlanche . Sched
 ule Ongoing All-Night Activities (7pm-7am) Paradise Exhibition Mitchell Ak
 iyama and Emma Nishimura JCCC Gallery 7:00 pm - 7:00 am Photo Spots 7:00 p
 m - 7:00 am Monument Unveiling Video 7:00 pm - 7:00 am Maru: Immigration S
 tories Audio Tour Self-Directed 7:00 pm - 7:00 am Activities Available Unt
 il 2am Food & Tea Sales 7:00 pm - 2:00 am Button Making 7:00 pm - 2:00 am 
 Tsukimi Origami 7:00 pm - 2:00 am Archival Station 7:00 pm - 2:00 am Gift 
 Shop 7:00 pm - 2:00 am Time Specific Events Paradise Artist Talk JCCC Gall
 ery 7:00 pm - 8:00 pm Building Tour 8:00 pm - 8:30 pm Frog Origami 9:00 pm
  - 10:00 pm Lantern Making workshop $10 fee payable at the workshop 10:00 
 pm - 11:00 pm Museum Tour 11:00 pm - 11:30 pm\n\nCategories: Community Eve
 nt\, JCCC Gallery\, Workshop
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
URL:https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/10/nuit-blanche-2026
X-SOURCE:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Issei Day 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261004T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261004T163000
UID:2945d1ce0810dfd7afca298b50932ffb@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:A Tribute to the Seniors of our Community The Board of Directo
 rs of the Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre extends an invitation to Issei
  Day on Sunday\, October 4\, 2026 \, and would like to welcome all who are
  70 years of age and older. This year will be the 64th year of celebrating
  Issei Day! We are so excited to welcome you back with a day full of activ
 ities\, with entertainment of songs and odori. As usual there will be a wo
 nderful and tasty bento and sweets served during intermission. To accommod
 ate everyone with seating and a bento\, we require that everyone pre-regis
 ter. Registration is now closed . It is wonderful to see so many of our se
 niors come to this event but there is a maximum capacity to ensure everyon
 e can sit\, relax and enjoy the afternoon\, so don’t delay - register to
 day! We look forward to seeing you. Date: Sunday\, October 4\, 2026 Time: 
 2pm - 4:30pm Venue: Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre (6 Sakura Way) Regis
 tration: Tuesday\, September 1 - Tuesday\, September 22\, 2026 Eligibility
 : For individuals aged 70 years and up\n\nCategories: Community Event
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
URL:https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/10/issei-day-2026
X-SOURCE:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paradise Opening Night Reception
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T160000
UID:a6e12617a0181c2dece986440238c643@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:In the multimedia exhibit\, Paradise \, which includes sculptu
 re\, print\, and video\, Japanese Canadian artists and childhood friends E
 mma Nishimura and Mitchell Akiyama grapple with their family histories of 
 internment. They consider how utopian worlds are created through resilienc
 e and displacement\, while urging us to remember that utopia for some may 
 not be utopia for all. Find out more about the exhibit here . Please join 
 us at our opening reception for a chance to take in this meaningful show a
 nd to meet the artists! Light refreshments will be served.\n\nCategories: 
 Community Event\, Social\, Exhibition
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
URL:https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/10/paradise-opening-night-reception
X-SOURCE:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aki no Tabi | 秋の旅
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T190000
UID:1e43949a1b1cd702dee939d13411dc35@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:Aki no Tabi — Autumn at the JCCC This fall\, join us at the 
 JCCC for a new seasonal experience celebrating Japanese and Japanese Canad
 ian culture through creativity\, connection\, and hands-on activities. Exp
 lore a variety of workshops and activities\, including: Wagashi-making\, C
 eramics\, Crochet\, and Journaling & paper craft workshops Craft activitie
 s Live music Food and drink vendors Local market vendors Inspired by the n
 ostalgic charm of Japan and the cozy feeling of autumn transitioning into 
 winter\, Aki no Tabi is a place to slow down\, create\, connect\, and enjo
 y the season together. Come experience the warmth and nostalgia of autumn 
 at the JCCC. 🍂 Keep an eye on this space for more detailed information 
 in the coming weeks!\n\nCategories: Community Event\, Social
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
URL:https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/11/aki-no-tabi
X-SOURCE:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Ishizue Award Dinner 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T210000
UID:347d8d1f18cfb5c9917f91900a7007a9@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:The JCCC Board of Directors is pleased to announce that the 8t
 h Ishizue Award and accompanying dinner will be held on Thursday November 
 19\, 2026. The Ishizue Award acknowledges and expresses our appreciation a
 nd respect to members or friends who have made exceptional contributions t
 o the Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre. The name Ishizue\, meaning corner
 stone or foundation\, pays tribute to the 75 families who\, at significant
  personal financial risk\, guaranteed the original mortgage on the JCCC at
  123 Wynford Drive in the early 1960’s. These families provided the foun
 dation upon which the JCCC was built\, and their support for the JCCC will
  forever be recognized as the cornerstone for who we are as a community. T
 he recipients of this annual award are a very distinguished group of peopl
 e who have each made significant life contributions to the Japanese Canadi
 an Cultural Centre. They are: Ken Fukushima Harry Kawabe Akiko Maruoka Dav
 id Ohashi (Post humous) Connie Sugiyama David Tsubouchi We cordially invit
 e you to honour these distinguished award recipients at an intimate and el
 egant dinner on Thursday November 19th at 6:30pm at the Japanese Canadian 
 Cultural Centre. Black tie optional. Tickets are $180 each (plus HST) . Ma
 ximum of 10 guests per table. To purchase tickets please order through the
  button below or in person at the JCCC\, starting September 21\, 2026\, an
 d ending November 9\, 2026. Please contact Sharon Marubashi for any furthe
 r information by email or phone (647-291-4751). On behalf of all of the di
 rectors of the Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre\, we look forward to spen
 ding a special evening of recognition and celebration together. Purchase T
